      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T07:32:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry to come back to this, but this is not inline with the objectives of the offload. I want to be able to respond the same offload packet for different service names and types. \nThis API does not reflect that. If I imagine how to use this API and want to make the same packet answer for 2 or more different {QNAMES,QTYPES} I\u0027ll do 2 calls with different mServiceNames. Which will result in 2 insertion with the same data, that is bad for memory by design. Do you expect the offload engine to check if the rawpacket is the same for 2 OffloadServiceInfo and merge them behind the scene ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 42,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "20ccb30e385927d9f7cc6d914af843f0174ec982",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "83953bac_4fa6e665",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/OffloadServiceInfo.java",
        "patchSetId": 21
      },
      "lineNbr": 42,
      "author": {
        "id": 1758351
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-05T07:45:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think the mRawOffloadPacket can be used to reply two different {QNAMES,QTYPES}. It basically only contains the PTR, SRV, TXT, A/AAAA record for single {QNAME, QTYPE}. If there are two different {QNAME, QTYPE} pair, it will be two different mRawOffloadPacket. We are not plan to merge two mRawOffloadPacket into one to make it contains multiple QNAME, QTYPE record.",
      "parentUuid": "44d70d37_306ade42",
